Pinned panda firmware
=====================

These files are the comma 3X panda firmware (H7) exactly as published on
sunnypilot's prebuilt `staging-c3x` branch. They are installed verbatim into
`panda/board/obj/` by `panda/SConscript` instead of being compiled.

Source:    origin/staging-c3x
Commit:    465accad0350169cd1fa80d7f78aa14f5cd8ba4e
Commit msg: bump to v2026.002.029
Vendored:  2026-10-16

Why pinned
----------
Compiling the panda firmware from source produces a per-commit, DEBUG-signed
image (`DEV-<short-commit>-DEBUG`, signed with `board/certs/debug`). Its RSA
signature changes on every build, so `pandad` re-flashes the panda on every
boot/update. The DEBUG source-built firmware is the suspected cause of the
dev-only cellular regression: flashing it appears to disturb the modem.

The pinned files are the exact signed release image the fleet runs, so `pandad`
never re-flashes. `panda_h7.bin.signed` keeps the same trailing 128-byte
signature block as the published release:

    Panda.get_signature_from_firmware(panda_h7.bin.signed)[:8].hex() == "406de22bd6d19eca"

`MANIFEST.sha256` records the sha256 of each file; `ci/agnos` verifies it.
